Patch 2505: shadow comparisons shift the reference by SHADOW_BIAS (default 0.02 of the light's depth range;
SHADOW_BIAS=0 = the exact compare as before).

J-Stars' characters (sleeves, hats, swords) showed grey stair-step lines and its plants shadows that moved with the
camera. A 4x shadow map (patch 2502), rounding the reference to the 24-bit depth format, a slope-scaled caster depth
bias and turning off vertex reuse did not remove them; the draw and copy order of both shadow maps is right and the
depth format is fixed-point. A shift of 0.02 removed them (0.002 did not), with shadows kept. A workaround: the v0.15
port and RPCS3 do not show the lines, so the cause is still open.

Tested (US disc): lines gone in a watched Free Battle at 0.02 (bench/exp/2026-11-09_0203-sh_bias02); Free Battle
29.79 flips/s with the default (bench/feature/2026-11-09_1958-bias02).

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c b/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
index ec4d8190..4b105414 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
@@ -512,12 +512,15 @@ u32 rsx_fp_texture_units(const u8* ucode, u32 max_bytes)
     return units;
 }
 
-/* SHADOW_BIAS=<float> (diagnostic, default 0): subtracted from the comparison reference, to measure how far the
- * stored depths sit from the references when a shadow comparison fails everywhere. */
+/* SHADOW_BIAS=<float>: subtracted from the comparison reference. Patch 2505: default 0.02 (SHADOW_BIAS=0 = the old
+ * exact compare). J-Stars' characters and plants showed grey stair-step lines and shadows that moved with the camera
+ * (self-shadowing); neither a 4x shadow map nor rounding the reference to the depth format nor a caster depth bias
+ * removed them, a reference shift of 0.02 of the light's depth range did (0.002 did not). A workaround until the
+ * cause is found; the v0.15 port and RPCS3 do not show them. */
 static const char* shadow_bias_txt(void)
 {
     static char b[32] = "";
-    if (!b[0]) { const char* e = getenv("SHADOW_BIAS"); snprintf(b, sizeof b, "%s", (e && *e) ? e : "0.0"); }
+    if (!b[0]) { const char* e = getenv("SHADOW_BIAS"); snprintf(b, sizeof b, "%s", (e && *e) ? e : "0.02"); }
     return b;
 }
 static void fp_shadow_helper(Out* p, u32 unit, u32 cube_mask,
